4x - 15 = 20 - 3x \implies 7x = 35 \implies x = 5\text{.}
\] Next, we calculate the length of the edge by substituting $x=5$ into either of the expressions: \[
4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\text{.}
\] Since the area of a square is the square of its side length, the area of this square is $5^2 = 25$ square meters.</think> <answer>$25$</answer>

